  'Separable tras "trotzdem": rief … an.': 'A separable verb after "trotzdem": rief … an.',
  'Ayer fue un día largo. Me dolía la cabeza, aun así fui al entrenamiento. El entrenador era duro, aun así me lo pasé bien. Aunque ya era tarde, después fuimos a cenar.': 'Yesterday was a long day. I had a headache, but I went to training anyway. The coach was strict, but it was fun anyway. Even though it was already late, we went out to eat afterwards.',
  'Los dos primeros huecos van con "trotzdem" y el verbo detrás; el tercero manda el verbo al final (war), y eso solo lo hace "obwohl".': 'The first two gaps take "trotzdem" with the verb after it; the third sends the verb to the end (war), and only "obwohl" does that.',
